                        "username": "rajeeranjan"
                    },
                    "message": "@unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com Can you share PLDM memory usage during firmware update both without and with this change?\n\nNormally this is how I capture the memory usage, but feel free to use any other method you prefer - \n\n```\nBefore starting Update-\nnohup top -b -d 0.1 | awk '{ print strftime(\"[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S]\"), $0; fflush(); }' > top_output.txt 2>&1 &\n\nOnce image is copied and pldm update starts\nkill %1\n\ncat top_output.txt | grep Mem:\n\ncat top_output.txt| grep /usr/bin/pldmd\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "@unive.tien.wiwynn@gmail.com This is a good optimization to have, but lets not add it as a pre-requisite for the firmware update feature. Once the firmware update patch series merge, we can come back to this. So, lets keep this patch after the firmware update patch in the series."
                }
